   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the Livingston\ncounty water and sewer authority",
    "basePrintNo": "S4037",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4037-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1199-gggg, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4037\n\nSPONSOR: HELMING\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the Living-\nston county water and sewer authority\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would increase the Livingston county water and sewer authori-\nty's statutory debt limit from $42,000,000 to $70,000,000.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 1 of section 1199-gggg of the public\nauthorities law to increase the aggregate principal amount of bonds,\nnotes, or other obligations the authority is allowed to issue from\n$42,000,000 to $70,000,000/\n\nSection 2: Provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation has been requested by both the Livingston County Board\nof Supervisors and the Livingston County Water and Sewer Authority. An\nincrease to the Authority's statutory debt limit is needed for the\nAuthority to complete current and future projects without deferment or\ndelay. The Authority is essential to ensuring vital services continue\nunabridged, such as the delivery of safe drinking water and sewer\nservices. Without this legislation to increase its debt limit, the\nAuthority's ability to upkeep the safe operation of existing systems\ncould be compromised.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
